### Table (standard ERP list)

- **First column**: The content of the **first column** (entity name / primary identifier: e.g. Contact Name, Customer Name, Proposal / Quote) must be **pegado al margen izquierdo** — use `text-left` for both `<th>` and `<td>`. Do not center the first column.
- **Other columns**: Use `text-center` for headers and cells so content is centered in the column. Use `<colgroup>` with explicit widths for homogeneous spacing (e.g. Directory, Proposals).
- **Labels/badges in center columns**: When a center-aligned cell contains a **label or badge** (e.g. `StatusBadge`, pill badges, or any `inline-flex` component), wrap the content in `<div className="flex justify-center">`. `text-center` alone does not reliably center inline-flex content; the wrapper ensures the label is visually centered in the cell and aligned with the column header. Apply this to all center columns that show status, payment, priority, or similar badges.
- **Actions column**: The **Actions** header and the action icons (View, Edit, Delete, etc.) must be **pegados al padding derecho** — use `text-right` for the Actions `<th>`, and `text-right` on the `<td>` with `justify-end` on the flex container so the last icon (e.g. Delete) sits against the right padding. This keeps the column visually consistent.
- **Padding**: Prefer `py-3 px-4` (headers) and `py-4 px-4` (cells); use `px-4` for consistent spacing.

```tsx
<div className="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden mb-4">
  <table className="table-fit">
    <colgroup>
      <col style={{ width: '14%' }} />
      {/* … */}
    </colgroup>
    <thead className="bg-gray-100 border-b border-gray-200">
      <tr>
        <th className="text-left py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900 text-xs">Name / ID</th>
        <th className="text-center py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900 text-xs">…</th>
        <th className="text-right py-3 px-4 font-medium text-gray-900 text-xs">Actions</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr className="border-b border-gray-100 hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors">
        <td className="py-4 px-4 text-gray-900 text-sm text-left">Primary text</td>
        <td className="py-4 px-4 text-center">
          <div className="flex justify-center">
            <StatusBadge status={order.status} type="salesOrder" size="sm" />
          </div>
        </td>
        <td className="py-4 px-4 text-gray-700 text-sm text-center">Plain text</td>
        <td className="py-4 px-4 text-right">…</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>
```

